  "design_notes": [
    "The \"Fact\" column is stored in twin. F38 is the fact-bank entry for terrain-relative navigation.",
    "Insertion errors are stored without the ± sign (±25 km is insertion_error_km 25). They are game values.",
    "\"+ Terrain-relative navigation\" is read as an add-on to the row above it (IMU + GNSS + star tracker), so add_on_to names that part. The design does not say whether it can extend the two cheaper options, or whether $6 M is the price of the add-on or of the whole set. It has no insertion error of its own; Core should take it from the part it extends.",
    "\"Landing ellipse −60%\" is a modifier on landing_ellipse_km.",
    "Terrain-relative navigation: \"Precision landing (C7, C8)\" with \"Mars/landing only\" is read as offered in C7 and C8 only. The other options carry no contracts list because the design does not restrict them.",
    "guidance_drift (8.4: \"IMU-only\") is listed only for IMU only.",
    "\"Drifts over time\", \"Less useful far beyond LEO\", \"Blinded near the Sun\", \"Needed for precise pointing & deep space\" and \"complex\" have no numbers; they are flags.",
    "The design gives no reliability for navigation sensors, so these parts do not roll."
  ],
